15. Dashboard Management Requirements

After publication, providers must be able to manage their business information through the existing Awasio dashboard.

Required management sections:

Interior Business Profile.
Branches and Locations.
Services and Specializations.
Materials and Brands.
Pricing and Packages.
Portfolio Projects.
Team Management.
Verification and Credentials.
Warranty and Support.
Interior Enquiries and Leads.
Reviews and Ratings.
Promotions and Boosts.

All information should be editable according to the provider's account permissions.

16. Product Rules

The following rules are considered finalized for version 1:

One Awasio account across all activities.
No separate interior designer login.
Existing Organization reused for companies.
Individual designers cannot add multiple branches.
Companies can add multiple branches.
Branches can configure services and prices independently.
Starting-price and material-package pricing are both supported.
Custom quotation-only pricing is supported.
Package inclusions and exclusions must be disclosed.
Material capabilities and actual project materials remain separate.
One approved completed project is mandatory for publication.
Verification badges require actual verification.
Company identity and branch-specific commercial information remain separate.
Existing property and flatmate workflows remain unchanged.
Existing Awasio credit wallet is reused.
